<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch gas production rose by 14.4 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Dutch gas production rose by 14.4 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Production of natural gas in the Netherlands rose by 14.4 percent in 1996, while oil production declined by 17.5 percent, the Dutch government said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Gas production rose by 11.3 billion cubic metres (bcm) to 89.6 bcm. Onshore production rose by 16.1 percent to 62.3 bcm, while offshore output was up 10.7 percent to 27.4 bcm.</p>
<p>Oil production fell by 0.56 million cubic metres (mcm) to 2.65 mcm in 1996, equivalent to 45,486 barrels per day.</p>
